ld re-classify as Archetype D/E\n(Product-Platform Hybrid / Option-Led); that re-classification is handled\ninside the failure scenario.\n\nENGINE 5 MODEL \u2014 MERGER ARBITRAGE EXPECTED VALUE\n\nDeal Payoff on Close:\n  Cash election: $90.00/share  [Actual \u2014 8-K]\n  Stock election: 0.3210 \u00d7 AMZN price, CAPPED at $90.00  [Actual \u2014 8-K]\n  AMZN reference price ~$252  [Actual \u2014 retrieved market data 2026-04-14]\n  \u2192 Stock election would be worth ~$80.89 at $252 AMZN  [Arithmetic]\n  Proration mechanics/Per Share Adjustment Amount: [Unconfirmed \u2014 merger\n  agreement detail beyond retrieved excerpt]\n  Blended close consideration: range $85.50-$87.50, central $87.00\n  [Estimate] (if 50-60% cash prorated, remainder stock at ~$81)\n  Effective discount to headline $90: -$3.00  [Estimate]\n\nTime to Close: expected 2027; assume 10 months (mid-2027) with range\n4-16 months  [Estimate \u2014 company says \"2027\"  [Actual]]\nDiscount Rate for Deal Payoff: 5.0% (risk-free 4.71% + ~0.3% deal-risk\npremium  [Assumption])\nPV of $87.00 at 5.0% for 10 months: 87.00 / (1.05)^0.833 = $83.50\n  [Arithmetic]\nPV of $90.00 at 5.0% for 10 months: $86.41  [Arithmetic]\n\nStandalone Failure Value (if deal terminated):\n  Pre-rumor market level (early April 2026): ~$65-69 (analyst mean target\n  $69.75 pre-announcement; stock had run +45% off YTD low of ~$48)\n  [Estimate \u2014 Barchart/Yahoo 2026-04-03]\n  Post-failure fundamental anchor: 20-25x revenue on $281M = $42-52/share\n  [Assumption]\n  Plus breakup fee if Amazon walks: +$4.57/share  [Actual \u2014 8-K]\n  Failure value range: $45-65; central $55  [Assumption]\n  (No breakup fee if regulators block  [Assumption \u2014 typical structure;\n  [Unconfirmed] exact trigger language beyond \"certain circumstances\"])\n\nProbability Distribution (Analyst Posterior):\n  P1 Deal closes on time (by end-2027): 78%  [Assumption]\n  P2 Deal closes delayed (2028): 12%  [Assumption]\n  P3 Deal closes at renegotiated lower price (~$85): 3%  [Assumption]\n  P4 Deal blocked by regulators (FCC/antitrust/CFIUS), no fee: 4%\n  [Assumption]\n  P5 Amazon walks (breakup fee paid): 2%  [Assumption]\n  P6 Competing/higher bid: 1%  [Assumption]\n  TOTAL = 100%\n\nScenario Values (at T0):\n  S1: $90 cash or mix \u2192 PV ~$86.41 (all cash) / $83.50 (blended $87)\n      Use blended: $83.50 \u00d7 78% = $65.13\n  S2: $90 delayed to 16 months \u2192 PV ~$84.30 (blended $87 \u2192 $81.50)\n      $81.50 \u00d7 12% = $9.78\n  S3: Renegotiated ~$85 at 12 months \u2192 PV ~$80.60\n      $80.60 \u00d7 3% = $2.42\n  S4: Regulatory block \u2192 standalone $50 (no fee)\n      $50 \u00d7 4% = $2.00\n  S5: Amazon walks \u2192 standalone $55 + $4.57 fee = $59.57\n      $59.57 \u00d7 2% = $1.19\n  S6: Competing bid $100 at 8 months \u2192 PV ~$96.80\n      $96.80 \u00d7 1% = $0.97\n\nEXPECTED VALUE (Probability-Weighted Intrinsic Value):\n  IV = $65.13 + $9.78 + $2.42 + $2.00 + $1.19 + $0.97 = $81.49\n  [Estimate \u2014 central]\n\nSensitivity (Tornado \u2014 \u00b11\u03c3 key variables):\n  1. Close probability P1 \u00b110pct (68-88%): IV range $76.10\u2013$86.90\n     \u2192 \u00b1$5.40/share  [Arithmetic]\n  2. Blended consideration \u00b1$2: IV range \u00b1$1.90  [Arithmetic]\n  3. Failure value \u00b1$10: IV range \u00b1$0.80  [Arithmetic]\n  Top-3 KPIs: (1) regulatory approval milestones, (2) cash/stock election\n  proration mechanics, (3) AMZN price trajectory vs $280.37.\n\nCross-check \u2014 Reverse Market-Implied Probability:\n  At price $82.36, if close value = $87 with PV $83.50 and failure = $55:\n  Implied P(close) = (82.36 - 55) / (83.50 - 55) = 27.36/28.50 = 96%\n  [Arithmetic]\n  At close value $90 PV $86.41 and failure $55: P = 27.36/31.41 = 87%\n  [Arithmetic]\n  \u2192 Market-implied close probability: 87-96%, consistent with the\n  analyst's 90-93% (P1+P2). NO MISPRICING.\n\nMargin of Safety:\n  MoS = (IV - Price)/IV = (81.49 - 82.36)/81.49 = -1.1%  [Arithmetic]\n  \u2192 Margin of Safety: NONE. Price \u2248 fair value, slightly above.\n\nReverse-DCF on Standalone Case (for completeness):\n  To justify $55 standalone, the market needs ~$330M revenue by 2030 with\n  12% EBIT margin (\u2248$40M EBIT), or a 20x multiple on $55M EBIT\n  [Assumption]. Feasible but aggressive for a company with a -$52M TTM\n  net income and negative owner earnings.\n\nENGINE 1/4 ALTERNATE CHECK (What if a different engine were used?):\n  A traditional DCF on standalone cash flows yields IV \u2248 $18-30/share\n  (revenue $300M, 10% EBIT margin by 2030, WACC 11%, growth 3%)\n  [Assumption].  Using a DCF here would be methodologically WRONG because\n  it ignores the deal's $90 fixed payoff \u2014 and would incorrectly suggest\n  the stock is wildly overvalued. The framework's \"No DCF-only\n  conclusions\" rule is honored.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive Response Simulation\n  If deal closes: Amazon/Globalstar D2D becomes vertically integrated with\n  Apple iPhones. SpaceX/Starlink (10,000+ sats, ~650 D2D sats vs GSAT 24\n  + 48 C-3), A