ied 87-96%. However, the $90 headline overstates\n  expected realized consideration (cash/stock proration likely results in\n  ~$87 at current AMZN prices), the 10-month wait discounts that to\n  ~$83.50, and the 10% failure branch carries a ~$27-37 downside. The\n  resulting probability-weighted intrinsic value of ~$81.49 is\n  essentially identical to the current price of $82.36. There is no\n  margin of safety and no positive expected risk-adjusted return; the\n  risk/reward asymmetry is poor (upside +$4.6 vs downside -$27). The\n  correct action is to own none of it at this price, and to re-engage\n  only if the deal spread materially widens on non-fundamental noise or\n  regulatory timeline delays that do not threaten close probability.\n\n  STRATEGY IF A POSITION IS REQUIRED (e.g., existing holder with tax\n  constraints):\n    \u2022 Hold \u22642% weight.\n    \u2022 Sell immediately into any narrowing of the spread below $84.00\n      (risk-adjusted return then clearly negative).\n    \u2022 Hedge the tail: long-dated AMZN puts (or short AMZN) to protect\n      the stock-election/protation component [Assumption \u2014 options\n      availability not confirmed].\n    \u2022 Exit entirely if any of these monitoring triggers fire:\n      (i) FTC complaint/DOJ lawsuit, (ii) FCC hearing designation,\n      (iii) launch delay beyond 2027Q2, (iv) merger agreement amendment\n      lowering consideration.\n\n  VOTE: AVOID / SELL (if held). No position at T0.\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nEND OF REPORT \u2014 RS2 v2.0 ANALYSIS \u2014 GSAT \u2014 T0 2026-08-24\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n```"}, {"sample": 2, "iv": null, "plausible": false, "reasons": ["no value extracted"], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "secs": 385, "report": "```markdown\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 RS2 v2.0 INTEGRATED INVESTMENT ANALYSIS \u2014 GLOBALSTAR, INC. (GSAT)\n\u25a0 T0: 2026-08-24 | Price: $82.36 | Mkt Cap: $10.671B | Shares: 129.5624M\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 0. ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\u25a0 Enterprise: GSAT \u2014 LEO satellite operator; 85% of network capacity dedicated to Apple under a long-term MSS agreement [Actual \u2014 SEC 10-Q, 2024-10-29].\n\u25a0 Dominant condition: Pending acquisition by Amazon (announced 2026-04-14 [Actual \u2014 Amazon press release]). All conventional going-concern valuation is subordinate to the deal. The stock has traded as a merger-arbitrage instrument since announcement.\n\u25a0 Engine selection (Layer 0): Archetype E (Option-Led / High-Beta). Blended Engine 4 (Expectation-Driven) \u00d7 40% for standalone franchise value + Engine 5 (Probability-Weighted Binary) \u00d7 60% for the merger event. Rationale: (1) ~97% of enterprise value is now a function of one binary event \u2014 the Amazon close; (2) GAAP cash-flow generation is negative, so traditional DCF yields a value far below any plausible market clearing price (see Layer 3); (3) the deal is structured as fixed $90.00 consideration with a 0.3210 AMZN stock alternative capped at $90.00 [Actual \u2014 Amazon release], converting the equity into a capped claim; (4) a pure Engine 1 DCF would be a category error for an event-driven equity.\n\u25a0 Model Confidence: MEDIUM-LOW. Key data gaps: capex [Unconfirmed], AMZN spot price for stock-leg valuation [Unconfirmed], FCC approval status [Unconfirmed], segment detail (zero dimensional lines in pack [Actual \u2014 pack declaration]).\n\u25a0 Bottom line pre-emption: Expected value \u2248 $84.70/share vs $82.36 price \u2192 MoS \u2248 2.8% [Estimate]. The spread is fair compensation for a 10-month, 10% binary break risk \u2014 nothing more. This is a risk-arbitrage trade, not an investment.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\nStep 1-1. Macro variables (as of Aug 2026):\n\u2022 10-yr UST: 4.702% (8/19/2026) [Actual \u2014 market data via bilyonaryo.com reprint of UST prices]\n\u2022 Fed funds: 3.50\u20133.75%; unchanged at July 2026 FOMC (5th consecutive hold); market pricing ~1/3 probability of a HIKE [Actual \u2014 Trading Economics]\n\u2022 Inflation/stagflation pressure: oil >$90 on Iran tanker strikes [Actual \u2014 European Business Magazine, Aug 2026]\n\u2022 DXY: drifting near multi-month lows [Actual \u2014 bilyonaryo 8/19/2026]\n\u2022 Credit spreads: no reliable series retrieved [Unconfirmed]\n\u2022 Economic cycle: late-cycle with inflation re-acceleration risk \u2014 policy stance \"hold-with-tightening-bias\"\nStep 1-2. Regime distribution [Estimate \u2014 my classification]:\n\u2022 Reflation (high rates + growth): 40%\n\u2022 Stagflation (high rates + slow growth): 25%\n\u2022 Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 25%\n\u2022 Recession (low rates + contraction): 10%\nStep 1-3. Sensitivity (each \u22123 to +3): interest rate sensitivity +1 (deal price fixed; opportunity cost of capital is the real channel); USD sensitivity \u22121 (modest non-US revenue); liquidity sensitivity 0 (event-driven, not flow-driven); cycle sensitivity \u22121 (Apple contract is counter-cyclical); commodity sensitivity +1 (satellite launch / MDA procurement cost embedded).\nStep 1-4. Macro alignment: EXPECTED MACRO IMPACT \u2248 0 \u2192 NEUTRAL. High rates erode the PV of a fixed $90 payment in 10\u201314 months (the spread is thin), but no macro variable materially alters the deal math. No conviction adjustment.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\nStep 1.5-1. Base rates:\n\u2022 Announced $1B+ US M&A completion rate: ~85\u201390% [Estimate \u2014 M&A transaction literature; framework reference]\n\u2022 Completion after HSR waiting period expires unchallenged: ~90%+ [Estimate \u2014 antitrust practice base rate]\n\u2022 Large-cap deal renegotiated lower post-signing: ~10\u201315% [Estimate]\n\u2022 Event-driven equity post-failure price vs pre-announcement price: typically \u221230% to \u221260% [Estimate \u2014 event study base rate]\nStep 1.5-2. Deviation from base rate: My total close probability (80%) is at/below the ~85\u201390% base rate. Justifications: (1) spectrum license transfer requires affirmative FCC approval with public-interest review [Actual \u2014 regulatory structure]; (2) Amazon's iRobot deal collapsed under regulatory pressure in 2024 \u2014 a demonstrated willingness of enforcers to challenge Big Tech [Estimate \u2014 public record]; (3) the deal entwines Amazon + Apple \u2014 the two largest consumer platforms \u2014 creating unusual political salience [Estimate \u2014 deal structure]. Deviation is adequately justified; no reversion to a higher base rate.\nStep 1.5-3. Base-rate shock check: my close probability (80%) is NOT >1.5\u00d7 the applicable base rate. No red flag.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (Buffett + Lynch)\nStep 2-1. What it does: Globalstar operates a low-earth-orbit satellite constellation providing voice, data, IoT and emergency messaging, monetized primarily through a wholesale capacity contract with Apple for iPhone/Apple Watch satellite services (85% of capacity allocated to Apple; Globalstar retains 100% of terrestrial/MSS revenue [Actual \u2014 SEC filing excerpt 2024-10-29]). It also serves ~260K direct subscribers [Estimate \u2014 research brief]. Understandability: MEDIUM.\nStep 2-2. Moat score: Intangible/spectrum 3; regulatory barriers 3; switching costs (Apple lock-in) 3; network scale 2; brand 1; data 1 \u2192 13/21 = WIDE MOAT as a strategic asset [Assumption \u2014 scored by me]. Moat direction: WIDENING for the combined Amazon+Apple network future; NARROWING for GSAT as an independent by 2028 as Amazon Leo D2D (2028 [Actual \u2014 Amazon release]) supersedes legacy capacity.\nStep 2-3. Lynch classification: TURNAROUND (standalone) / ASSET PLAY (spectrum) \u2014 but correctly: a Special Situation merger arb.\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard:\n\u2022 Revenue 5-yr CAGR: +16.3% [Arithmetic on filed data]; TTM revenue $0.281B, +9% FY2025 [Actual]\n\u2022 Operating margin: FY2025 +2.7% (first positive year); 12-yr median \u221250.7% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 ROE: \u221215.9% [Aggregator]; GAAP net income TTM \u2212$0.052B [Actual]\n\u2022 OCF FY2025 $0.622B vs net income \u2212$0.009B: the OCF is inflated by Apple upfront/prepaid capacity payments [Actual \u2014 Yahoo Finance report] and SBC add-back; this is NOT recurring owner earnings\n\u2022 Accruals ratio \u22120.3123 [Arithmetic] confirms earnings are far below cash \u2014 deferred/prepaid revenue phenomenon\n\u2022 Net debt: cash $0.447B [Actual] + marketable securities [Unconfirmed \u2014 not extracted] vs LT debt $0.452B + current portion $0.032B [Actual] = net debt \u2248 +$0.037B (near zero); operating leases +$0.063B disclosed, excluded from debt (treated as operating expense) [my choice, disclosed]\n\u2022 Interest coverage: op income $7.4M [Actual] vs est. interest ~$28\u201336M on $0.484B debt at 6\u20137.5% [Assumption] \u2192 <1\u00d7. CONCERNING.\nOverall: WEAK standalone economics; ADEQUATE strategic balance sheet (zero net debt).\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u20133 each): buyback 0; M&A 0 (no track record); capex efficiency 1 (constellation build-out unproven, current returns negative); mix rationality 2 (Apple prepayments fund contracted capacity \u2014 rational); guidance accuracy 3 (FY2025 revenue in line with guidance [Actual]; guidance suspended post-merger [Actual \u2014 web sources]). Subtotal 6/15. Insider bonus: CEO/mgmt >5% +1 (insiders 59.46% [Aggregator]); current insider transactions = sale to Amazon (neutral) \u2192 Total 7/15.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\nStep 2.5-1. R&D: XCOM RAN development expensed in opex [Actual \u2014 Q4 2025 call]; no reliable split \u2192 not capitalized [Unconfirmed]. \nStep 2.5-2. SBC: FY2025 $0.023B = 8.4% of revenue [Actual]. Adjusted FCF = OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC. Since OCF is prepayment-inflated: Normalized OCF \u2248 NI + D&A \u2212 \u0394WC \u2212 SBC = \u22120.009 + 0.087 \u2212 (\u22120.015) \u2212 0.023 \u2248 +$0.040B [Arithmetic] \u2014 before capex. With capex [Unconfirmed] implied at ~$0.3\u20130.5B/yr (PP&E rose +$0.63B in FY2025 [Arithmetic]), true FCF is deeply negative.\nStep 2.5-3. Operating leases: $0.063B [Actual] \u2014 excluded from debt.\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC: negative on both GAAP and adjusted basis [Estimate]; the P/L gap vs GAAP is minor here.\nStep 2.5-6. Owner earnings (Buffett): NI \u2212$9M + D&A $87M \u2212 maintenance capex est. $40M \u2212 \u0394WC +15M [all Arithmetic/Assumption] \u2248 +$20\u201340M ONLY if maintenance capex is at the low end and Apple prepayments continue. If the constellation build-out is real growth capex, owner earnings are negative. Conclusion: the \"record OCF\" of $0.572\u20130.622B is a working-capital phenomenon, not compounding power.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 3. VALUATION ENGINE (Blended Engine 4 \u00d7 40% + Engine 5 \u00d7 60%)\nDeal facts [Actual \u2014 Amazon press release 2026-04-14; MLex 2026-07-17]:\n\u2022 Consideration: $90.00 cash OR 0.3210 AMZN shares, value capped at $90.00/share\n\u2022 Cash elections capped at 40% of total shares; excess cash elections convert to stock (proration)\n\u2022 Aggregate consideration \u2248 $11.57B; premium 23.5% over pre-announcement close (implies pre-deal price \u2248 $72.85 [Arithmetic])\n\u2022 Majority stockholder approved by written consent [Actual \u2014 company Q1 2026 release]\n\u2022 US HSR waiting period expired WITHOUT suit on 2026-07-17 [Actual \u2014 MLex]\n\u2022 Expected close: 2027 [Actual \u2014 company release]; I use a midpoint of ~10 months from T0 \u2192 mid-2027 [Assumption]\n\u2022 AMZN spot price [Unconfirmed \u2014 not retrievable before budget exhaustion]; analyst targets $305\u2013318 [Estimate \u2014 Yahoo Finance]. IF AMZN \u2265 $280.37, the 0.3210 stock leg = $90.00 (cap binds). Threshold for the blended value (40% cash + 60% stock) to exceed T0 price: AMZN \u2265 $240.72 [Arithmetic].\n\nStep 3-1. Standalone DCF (Engine 4 layer, for break-scenario calibration):\nExplicit forecast (break-case standalone, my assumptions \u2014 the weakest link, flagged):\n| Year | Revenue ($B) [Assumption] | EBITDA margin [Assumption] | EBITDA ($B) | Capex ($B) [Assumption] | FCF ($B) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | 0.295 (+8%) | 35% | 0.103 | 0.400 | \u22120.350 |\n| 2027E | 0.320 (+10%) | 36% | 0.115 | 0.300 | \u22120.220 |\n| 2028E | 0.350 (+10%) | 37% | 0.130 | 0.100 | +0.005 |\n| 2029E | 0.378 (+8%) | 38% | 0.145 | 0.080 | +0.040 |\n| 2030E | 0.405 (+7%) | 40% | 0.162 | 0.080 | +0.055 |\n2026-27 revenue growth anchors: Q1 2026 +17% [Actual], Q2 2026 \u22123.5% [Actual], FY2025 +9% [Actual]; post-2028 deceleration as Amazon Leo D2D [Actual 2028 deployment] competes with legacy Globalstar. WACC: 4.70% rf [Actual] + 1.514 beta [Aggregator] \u00d7 5.0% ERP [Assumption] \u2248 12.3% \u2192 use 11% blended with lower-scale premium [Assumption]. Terminal growth 2.5% [Assumption].\nPV of FCF 2026\u201330 \u2248 \u2212$0.44B; TV = 0.055\u00d71.025/(0.11\u22120.025) = $0.663B \u2192 PV \u2248 $0.39B; EV \u2248 \u2212$0.04B; add net cash $0.037B \u2192 equity \u2248 $0.0\u20130.1B. Pure cash-flow value \u2248 $0\u20131/share [Estimate].\nInterpretation: The DCF is a category failure for this asset class \u2014 it prices only cash flows, not spectrum scarcity, the 85%-capacity Apple franchise, or a strategic buyer's synergies. I retain it in the report to show that the $35\u201365 break-range rests entirely on strategic-asset premiums, NOT on earnings power. This is the critical model weakness and is carried into scenario widths.\n\nStep 3-2. Probability-weighted merger EV (Engine 5 \u2014 the primary engine):\n| Scenario | Probability [Estimate] | Per-share value ($) | EV contribution ($) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1. Close at $90, mid-2027 | 70% | 90.00 | 63.00 |\n| 2. Close at $90, delayed to 2028 | 10% | 84.00 (PV @9%) | 8.40 |\n| 3. Close at reduced consideration (AMZN < $280 or renegotiation ~$85) | 10% | 85.00 | 8.50 |\n| 4. Deal breaks; standalone trading | 10% | 48.00 (60% CI: 35\u201365) | 4.80 |\n| TOTAL | 100% | Expected Price | $84.70 |\nProbability anchors: base rate post-HSR \u2248 90% [Estimate]; my 80% total close is conservative; break value 48 = 0.35\u00d765 (second-bidder path, e.g., Apple or PE [Assumption]) + 0.65\u00d735 (strategic-standalone drift [Assumption]).\n\nStep 3-3. Reverse DCF (market-implied): At $82.36, with break value $48, market-implied close probability = (82.36\u221248)/(90\u221248) = 81.8% [Arithmetic]. My model says 80% close. The market is pricing the SAME odds I am \u2014 within noise. No free lunch.\n\nStep 3-4. Tornado (\u00b11\u03c3 on the top 3 variables):\n1. Close probability 70% \u00b110 \u2192 EV $80.5\u201388.9 (\u0394\u00b1$4.2) \u2190 THE driver\n2. Break value $48 \u00b115 \u2192 EV $83.2\u201386.2 (\u0394\u00b1$1.5)\n3. Time to close 10 mo \u00b16 \u2192 IRR 11.2% vs 7.9% gross (\u0394\u00b13.3% annualized)\nThesis KPI = FCC approval milestone (drives close probability).\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2022 Competitive response: if the deal closes, Amazon becomes the D2D anchor (Apple + Amazon), intensifying pressure on AST SpaceMobile/Starlink D2C \u2014 validates the spectrum thesis but does not change GSAT shareholder value (capped at $90) [Estimate].\n\u2022 Reflexivity: GSAT share price cannot improve the deal (fixed consideration). Declining AMZN < $241 makes the mixed consideration worth less than the GSAT price \u2014 a reflexive negative loop only in the stock-election tail [Arithmetic].\n\u2022 Customer evolution: Apple iPhone users unaffected; agreement survives via the Amazon\u2013Apple contract [Actual]. The 260K legacy subscriber base is immaterial to the deal.\n\u2022 Integration risk: MD Space liquidated-damages provision noted [Actual \u2014 10-Q]; satellite delivery delays are a deal-timing risk, not a value risk.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2