u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Headline: GSAT is the subject of a definitive $90.00/share merger with Amazon\n  (announced 2026-04-14; stockholder approval already secured via Thermo's written\n  consent; close expected in 2027). At T0 the stock trades at 91.5% of the deal\n  price, i.e. the market has already priced in a ~90-95% completion probability.\n  My independent completion probability is ~85%, and my standalone intrinsic value\n  ($24/share base) is far below the deal price. Expected value \u2248 $75-78 vs $82.36.\n  \u2192 Margin of Safety NEGATIVE (-6% to -10%). No new capital should be deployed.\n\u2022 Enterprise Archetype: E \u2014 Option-Led / High-Beta, in a deal-induced transition\n  state. Valuation Engine: Engine 4 (Expectation-Driven) for standalone value,\n  nested with Engine 5 (Probability-Weighted Binary) for the acquisition outcome,\n  which dominates the current market value. Post-close the public equity ceases to\n  exist; if the deal fails, GSAT reverts to Option-Led standalone economics.\n\u2022 Data posture: Deal terms, guidance and merger timeline are sourced from primary\n  and secondary web research ([Actual]/[Estimate]); all standalone forecast drivers\n  beyond 2026 guidance are my own [Assumption] and are flagged as such, with\n  explicit sensitivity analysis because the company has suspended forward guidance\n  pending the merger (no 2027+ company numbers exist).\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 1-1. Macro variables (as of 2026-08-21/24):\n\u2022 10Y UST: 4.74% (FRED DGS10, 2026-08-21) [Actual]; +0.44pt YoY, direction: rising.\n\u2022 Real rate: ~2.0% (10Y nominal 4.74% less ~2.7% inflation proxy) [Estimate].\n\u2022 Fed funds target: 3.50-3.75%, on hold 5th consecutive meeting (Jul-2026); markets\n  price ~1-in-3 odds of a HIKE (TradingEconomics) [Estimate]. Stance: restrictive-hold.\n\u2022 DXY: ~98.6, -2.4% in the month (TradingEconomics, 2026-08-20) [Estimate]; weak/falling dollar.\n\u2022 Credit spreads: not retrieved \u2014 [Unconfirmed]; assumed benign-to-widening given\n  restrictive Fed and a risk-off tone into gold/crypto (Daily Caller, 2026-08-21) [Estimate].\n\u2022 Global liquidity: tightening bias; dollar weakness suggests non-USD liquidity flows.\n\u2022 Cycle position: late expansion with stagflationary undertones; markets pricing a\n  hike despite soft dollar \u2014 an unusual, policy-stressed regime.\n\nStep 1-2. Regime probability distribution (must sum to 100%):\n  Reflation (high rates + growth):        30%\n  Stagflation (high rates + low growth):  30%\n  Goldilocks (low rates + growth):        25%\n  Recession (low rates + low growth):     15%\n  TOTAL: 100%\n\nStep 1-3. GSAT macro sensitivity (each -3..+3):\n  Interest-rate sensitivity:  +2.5  (long-duration, capex-heavy; 10Y at 4.74% and rising)\n  Dollar sensitivity:         +0.5  (revenue ~all USD from Apple; global opex minor)\n  Liquidity sensitivity:      +2.0  (standalone model depends on prepayment/debt/equity access)\n  Economic-cycle sensitivity: +0.5  (contracted wholesale; emergency services are non-cyclical)\n  Commodity sensitivity:      +0.5  (launch costs via MDA/SpaceX, minor)\n\nStep 1-4. Macro alignment: Regime-Weighted Expected Macro Impact \u2248 -0.6\u03c3 \u2192 Headwind\n  (moderate). The dominant macro risk is rates: at 4.74% with a hawkish Fed, the\n  long-duration satellite cash flows are discounted harder, and standalone capital\n  access (which the deal conveniently removes) is expensive. Macro alignment:\n  Conviction -0.5 steps,