s\n  framework M&A base rate \u224888% \u2192 ratio <1.5x, no flag. If the bull case assumed\n  p>95% completion AND full standalone optionality re-rate post-close, that would\n  exceed 1.5x base rate and require extra evidence \u2014 it is not assumed here.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (Buffett + Lynch)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2-1. Business understanding (3 sentences):\n  1) GSAT operates a low-earth-orbit mobile-satellite-services (MSS) network and\n     licenses its 2.4 GHz \"Band 53/n53\" terrestrial spectrum, monetized primarily\n     through wholesale capacity contracts \u2014 the largest being Apple's Emergency SOS,\n     Messages, Find My and Roadside Assistance services on iPhone/Apple Watch\n     (wholesale = ~68% of revenue, run-rate \u2248 $185M/yr).\n  2) It is building a next-generation 54-satellite constellation (manufactured by\n     MDA Space), financed largely by Apple prepayments (cap raised to $1.58B in\n     Apr-2026), which will extend D2D capacity through ~2035 and enable future\n     MNO/enterprise D2D wholesale.\n  3) Amazon agreed (Apr-2026) to acquire GSAT for $90/share cash-or-stock (~$11.6B)\n     to fold its spectrum, fleet and Apple relationship into Amazon Leo D2D; the\n     merger is expected to close in 2027.\n  Understandability: Medium-High (the contract is simple; the constellation buildout\n  and prepayment accounting are not). No downgrade, but see Section 2.5.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat assessment (0-3 each) + direction:\n  Intangible assets (brand/licences): 2  \u2014 FCC MSS + Band 53 exclusive licences [Actual]\n  Switching costs:                    2  \u2014 Apple SOS deeply integrated into iOS; carrier-grade ops\n  Network effects:                    1  \u2014 modest; constellation coverage improves with fleet\n  Cost advantage:                     1  \u2014 small scale vs SpaceX/AST\n  Economies of scale:                 1  \u2014 not yet realized (loss-making)\n  Regulatory barriers:                3  \u2014 spectrum + satellite licensing is the real moat\n  Data moat:                          1  \u2014 usage data from SOS/IoT, minor\n  TOTAL: 11/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT (low end).\n  Moat direction: NARROWING as a standalone (competitors AST SpaceMobile, Iridium,\n  Starlink D2C encroach; Apple holds the customer relationship and could dual-source)\n  but the moat is being TRANSFERRED to Amazon, not dissolved. Direction judged on the\n  standalone entity: Stable-to-Narrowing.\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch classification: Turnaround/Asset Play hybrid (contract-backed\n  cash-flow story + spectrum asset). Checkpoints: spectrum realizable value\n  ([Estimate] $0.4-0.9B), Apple contract durability (strong, contract through ~2035),\n  path to GAAP profitability (not visible standalone before ~2029).\n\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard (pack data, [Filed]):\n  Revenue growth: FY25 +9.2% [Arithmetic]; 3-yr CAGR 22.4% [Arithmetic]; 5-yr 16.3% [Arithmetic]; TTM +2.9%; Q2-26 -3.5% YoY (decelerating)\n  Operating margin: FY25 +2.7% vs 12-yr median -50.7% [Arithmetic] \u2014 huge improvement, still thin\n  Net income: FY25 -$9M; TTM -$52M [Filed] \u2014 Q2-26 loss widened to -$27M\n  ROE: GAAP -2.5% (FY25, NI/avg equity) [Arithmetic]; vendor TTM -15.9% [Aggregator]\n  FCF margin: negative (OCF $622M \u2212 est. capex ~$700M \u2248 -$78M FY25) [Arithmetic + Assumption]\n  Net debt/EBITDA: \u2248 0.4x (net debt \u2248 $37M; EBITDA \u2248 $94M) [Arithmetic]\n  Interest coverage: \u2248 0.2x (EBIT $7.4M / est. interest ~$36M) [Assumption \u2014 interest not in pack]\n  Net cash/(debt): \u2248 -$37M net debt (LT debt $452M + current $32M \u2212 cash $447M) [Arithmetic on pack]\n  VERDICT: ADEQUATE structure (cash + prepayments + contracted revenue) but\n  WEAK profitability; the balance sheet is prepayment-funded, not organically funded.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0-3 each):\n  Buyback efficiency:  0 \u2014 no buybacks; heavy SBC dilution history (shares 934M\u21921.8B pre-split 2014-2022)\n  M&A track record:    1 \u2014 spectrum purchases (n53) sensible; no history of value-accretive M&A\n  Capex efficiency:    1 \u2014 constellation capex is strategic but unproven; incremental ROIC < WACC to date\n  Mix rationality:     2 \u2014 prepayment financing (Apple) is rational and low-cost; but reliance on one customer\n  Guidance accuracy:   3 \u2014 revenue guidance hit/beat 2024 and 2025 (\"fourth consecutive year of record revenue\" [Actual])\n  Subtotal: 7/15. Insider bonus: management+Thermo+Apple \u2248 59.5% ownership [Aggregator] \u2192 +1.\n  TOTAL: 8/15 \u2014 fair, not compelling.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n2.5-1. R&D capitalization: XCOM RAN + next-gen D2D R&D is inside SG&A/opex (pack\n  shows no separate R&D line; [Unconfirmed] magnitude, small vs $273M revenue).\n  Capitalizing it (~$15-25M/yr assumed) raises adjusted EBIT by ~$10-15M \u2014 immaterial.\n2.5-2. SBC treatment: deduct from cash flow. FY25 SBC $23M, FY24 $36M [Filed].\n  Adjusted FCF FY25 \u2248 OCF $622M \u2212 est. capex $700M \u2212 SBC $23M \u2248 -$101M [Assumption+Filed].\n  Owner earnings (Buffett): NI -$9M + D&A $87M \u2212 maintenance capex (est. $60M) \u2212 \u0394WC\n  (+$15M use, FY25) \u2212 SBC $23M \u2248 -$20M [Assumption-heavy]. The business does NOT yet\n  earn its keep on a cash basis; the $622M OCF is a prepayment artifact, not earnings.\n2.5-3. Operating leases: $63M (FY25) [Filed] \u2014 capitalize at ~8x \u2192 ~$0.5B-equivalent\n  burden is immaterial vs a $10.7B market cap; adjusted net debt still \u2248 +$0.1B.\n2.5-4. Brand/data: SOS brand value modest; data asset = 260k IoT subs + SOS usage \u2014\n  not separately monetizable; [Assumption] ~$0.\n2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC: NEGATIVE (adjusted NOPAT < $0). GAAP ROIC also negative.\n  No gap analysis needed beyond: GAAP is impaired by $87M D&A on a prepayment-funded\n  fleet; adjusted economics are slightly better but still sub-WACC. This is an\n  infrastructure company, not a software compounder.\n2.5-6. Owner earnings \u2248 -$20M (FY25) [Assumption-heavy]. Even generous treatment\n  (excluding SBC and using adjusted EBITDA) gives \u2248 +$71M before capex \u2014 and capex\n  consumes it all. KEY TAKEAWAY: all value rests on the contracted prepayments and\n  the deal, not on current organic cash generation.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 3. VALUATION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nEngine selection (Layer 0, 0-2..0-4): Archetype E (Option-Led/High-Beta) with Engine 4\n  (Expectation-Driven) for the standalone entity, nested with Engine 5\n  (Probability-Weighted Binary) for the dominant acquisition outcome.\n  Reasons: (a) >90% of current market value is the fixed $90 merger consideration \u2014\n  a binary outcome; (b) standalone GAAP/FCF economics are negative and all optional\n  value (spectrum, D2D, Apple renewal) is option-like; (c) a conventional DCF alone\n  would mis-price a company whose cash flows are prepayment-timed. Error check: using\n  Engine 1 (DCF-only) would produce ~$9-24/share and wrongly imply the stock is 70%\n  overvalued even if the deal closes; using Engine 3 (platform hybrid) would overpay\n  for \"installed base\" that belongs to Apple's iOS, not GSAT. Transition state: YES \u2014\n  Option-Led \u2192 (acquisition). Transition criteria \"50-80% met\" apply: the deal is\n  signed, consent delivered, Apple agreements amended; >80% of the transition to a\n  private Amazon subsidiary is mechanically complete. Per framework, Conviction -0.5.\n\nStep 3-A. DEAL VALUE (Engine 5 \u2014 the dominant scenario):\n  Consideration: $90.00/share cash, or 0.3210 AMZN shares with value capped at $90;\n  40% aggregate cash cap with proration; potential milestone-related adjustments\n  [Actual \u2014 aboutamazon.com merger release, 2026-04-14; TradingView 8-K summary,\n  [Estimate] for the milestone clause].\n  Premium: 23.5% over 2026-04-13 close \u2192 pre-deal price \u2248 $72.87 [Arithmetic].\n  Timeline: close expected 2027, subject to regulatory approvals [Actual \u2014\n  Businesswire Q1-2026 release]. Remaining conditions: FCC licence transfer consent,\n  HSR, other clearances; stockholder approval DONE (Thermo written consent [Estimate \u2014\n  8-K summary]).\n  Close-case value: $90 less milestone-adjustment risk \u2192 base $88 (range $85-90).\n  PV at rf 4.74% [Actual]: 9 months \u2248 $86.9; 15 months \u2248 $82.2.\n\nStep 3-B. STANDALONE VALUE (Engine 4 \u2014 the failure-case anchor):\n  Explicit 10-year forecast (all items USD M; 2026E revenue = guidance midpoint;\n  all post-2026 drivers are MY [Assumption] because the company has suspended\n  forward guidance pending the merger [Estimate \u2014 research brief]):\n\n  Year    Rev    EBITDAm%  EBITDA   D&A    EBIT    Capex   \u0394WC     FCF\n  2026E   292    35%       102      110    -8      500     -200    -198\n  2027E   330    37%       122      135    -13     250     -100    -28\n  2028E   372    39%       145      160    -15     120     0       +25\n  2029E   408    41%       167      175    -8      80      0       +87\n  2030E   440    43%       189      185    +4      75      0       +114\n  2031E   468    44%       206      185    +21     70      0       +136\n  2032E   492    45%       221      180    +41     68      0       +153\n  2033E   512    45%       230      170    +60     66      0       +164\n  2034E   528    46%       243      160    +83     65      0       +178\n  2035E   540    46%       248      150    +98     65      0       +183\n\n  DRIVER SOURCING (mandatory):\n  \u2022 2026E revenue $292M: company guidance $280-305M [Estimate \u2014 TipRanks aggregator\n    of company guidance; consistent with Q1-26 $70.1M +17% [Actual \u2014 Globalstar IR]\n    and Q2-26 -3.5% [Actual \u2014 filed 10-Q]).\n  \u2022 2027E-2035E growth (13% \u2192 2.3%): MY [Assumption]; anchored on D2D wholesale\n    ramp + Apple contract through ~2035 (85% capacity reservation) then deceleration;\n    NO company guidance exists beyond 2026. Show sensitivity below.\n  \u2022 EBITDA margin 35% (2026E) \u2192 46% (2035E): FY25 actual unadjusted 34.4%\n    [Arithmetic]; 2026 guidance ~50% is ADJUSTED (adds back SBC ~$23M and other\n    non-cash items) [Estimate]; my model uses the conservative UNADJUSTED basis.\n  \u2022 D&A $110M \u2192 $150M: FY25 actual $87M [Filed]; rises with ~$1.5B constellation\n    (net PP&E +$631M in FY25 [Arithmetic]) \u2014 [Assumption].\n  \u2022 Capex $500M (2026E) \u2192 $65M (2035E): FY25 implied ~$700M [Assumption on\n    Arithmetic]; 2026 guided capex NOT found in research \u2192 [Unconfirmed], my\n    $500M is an [Assumption]; maintenance $65-70M later [Assumption].\n  \u2022 \u0394WC: -$200M/-$100M (2026-27) = remaining Apple prepayment draws (cap lifted\n    $468M to $1.58B Apr-2026 [Estimate \u2014 8-K summary]); then ~0 [Assumption].\n  \u2022 Cash taxes: $0 through 2035 (NOL shield from -$2.137B retained earnings\n    [Filed]) \u2014 [Assumption].\n  \u2022 Terminal: FCF 2036 $188M, g=2.5% [Assumption \u2264 long-run nominal GDP].\n  \u2022 WACC 10.5% [Assumption \u2014 derivation below].\n  PV of FCFs (10.5%, t=1..10): -198\u2192-179; -28\u2192-23; 25\u219219; 87\u219258; 114\u219269;\n  136\u219275; 153\u219276; 164\u219274; 178\u219272; 183\u219268 \u2192 \u03a3 PV FCF \u2248 +$309M.\n  TV = 188/(0.105-0.025) = $2,345M; PV(TV) = $865M. EV \u2248 $1,174M.\n  Plus net cash/(debt) \u2248 -$37M [Arithmetic] \u2192 Equity \u2248 $1,137M \u2192 \u2248 $8.8/share.\n  This is the CONSERVATIVE contract-only bookend.\n\n  WACC derivation: rf = 10Y 4.74% [Actual, FRED]; ERP 4.5% [Assumption]; vendor\n  beta 1.514 [Aggregator \u2014 window unstated]; standalone beta \u22481.3 [Assumption, deal\n  overhang inflates the vendor beta]; CoE = 4.74% + 1.3\u00d74.5% \u2248 10.6%. Cost of debt\n  8.0% pre-tax [Assumption \u2014 GSAT credit, interest not in pack]; tax 0% (NOL)\n  [Assumption]; weights E 87% / D 13% (standalone equity ~$3-4B vs debt $0.48B)\n  [Assumption]. WACC \u2248 0.87\u00d710.6% + 0.13\u00d78.0% \u2248 10.3% \u2192 round to 10.5% for\n  satellite/execution risk [Assumption].\n\n  SOTP cross-check (my [Estimate]/[Assumption] anchors):\n  Apple wholesale contract PV (contracted net cash, prepayments already received):\n      $1.0-1.3B   [Estimate \u2014 Q1-26 wholesale $46.3M run-rate \u00d710yr \u00d7 margin, PV @10%]\n  Spectrum (Band 53/n53 US terrestrial + MSS licences): $0.4-0.9B [Estimate \u2014\n      ~11.5MHz 2.4GHz TDD \u00d7 ~350M POPs at ~$0.10-0.23/MHz-POP, heavily discounted]\n  Legacy IoT/SPOT/duplex: $0.25-0.4B [Estimate \u2014 ~$80M revenue, ~10x EBITDA]\n  Third-party D2D optionality post-2028: $0-1.2B [Assumption]\n  Net cash/(debt): -$0.04B [Arithmetic]\n  \u2192 Equity range $1.6-3.8B = $12-29/share; BASE \u2248 $24/share.\n\n  STANDALONE INTRINSIC VALUE (my judgment): BASE $24/share.\n  50% CI: $15-35 | 80% CI: $8-50. [Assumption-heavy \u2014 Tier 4/5 dependence:\n  contract cash split, spectrum value, D2D optionality are all unverifiable \u2192 Model\n  Confidence DOWNGRADED to Moderate.]\n\nStep 3-C. Tornado sensitivity (top-3 variables driving total value):\n  \u00b11\u03c3 in each, around the blended EV:\n  1. Deal completion probability p (85% \u00b1 7pp): EV \u00b1 ~$5\n  2. Standalone value ($24 \u00b1 $16): EV \u00b1 ~$2.5 (weighted by 15% failure branch)\n  3. 2026-27 capex ($500M/250M \u00b1 40%): EV \u00b1 ~$1.5\n  \u2192 THESIS KPI #1 = regulatory/deal milestones; #2 = Apple prepayment drawdowns;\n  #3 = constellation launch schedule (MDA).\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3.5-1. Competitive response: If the Amazon-GSART D2D succeeds, SpaceX/Starlink D2C\n  and AST SpaceMobile accelerate; Amazon's entry is itself the disruption (-2 on a\n  -3..+3 scale for GSAT-as-standalone; irrelevant to holders post-close).\n3.5-2. Reflexivity: HIGH stock price \u2192 cheap AMZN stock currency for the deal and\n  SBC-free hiring; if the deal BREAKS, the reflexivity flips violently negative \u2014\n  talent loss, Apple renegotiation leverage, funding stress. This is the mechanism\n  that would take a broken-deal GSAT well below $24 (hence the $8 tail scenario).\n3.5-3. Customer evolution: SOS (early-adopter, ~free with iPhone) \u2192 paid messaging/\n  roadside (mainstream) \u2192 MNO wholesale D2D (late). As penetration grows, churn\n  stays near-zero for Apple-subsidized features but LTV/CAC economics shift from\n  Apple-funded to MNO-funded \u2014 the unproven monetization step.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIOS (Bayesian)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior (Layer 1.5 base rates): deal-completion ~88%; D2D success ~20-30%.\nUpdate triggers observed (Bayesian likelihood update):\n  + Stockholder approval delivered (Thermo) \u2014 likelihood \u2191\n  + Apple prepayment cap raised + SOW amended + Licensee-stake sale agreed \u2014 likelihood \u2191\n  + Amazon-Apple services agreement signed \u2014 likelihood \u2191\n  + No antitrust objection reported as of Aug-2026 \u2014 likelihood \u2191\n  - FCC licence-transfer consent NOT yet granted \u2014 likelihood \u2193 (timing)\n  - Q2-26 net loss widened to -$27M (weak standalone) \u2014 no effect on deal, \u2193 standalone\nPosterior scenario set (probabilities sum to 100%; base case = highest single):\n\n  S1 \u2014 Deal closes on time, full consideration (p=45%):\n       Receive $90 (PV \u2248 $86.9 at ~9 mo). Standalone irrelevant. Price ~$90.\n  S2 \u2014 Deal closes delayed/adjusted (p=40%):\n       Close 12-18 mo, consideration $85-90 after milestone adjustments (PV \u2248 $82.2\n       at ~15 mo). Price $85-90.\n  S3 \u2014 Deal breaks; standalone continues (p=12%):\n       Value = standalone base $24 (50% CI 15-35). Price re-rates to ~$15-35.\n  S4 \u2014 Deal breaks + Apple/strategy impairment (p=3%):\n       Value \u2248 $8 (dilutive funding, spectrum distress, SOS contract renegotiation).\n  TOTAL = 100%. P(deal closes) = 85% (my estimate; market-implied \u2248 92-95% \u2014 see 4.5).\n\nExpected value (T0):\n  EV = 0.45\u00d786.9 + 0.40\u00d782.2 + 0.12\u00d724 + 0.03\u00d78 = 39.1 + 32.9 + 2.9 + 0.2 \u2248 $75.1\n  EV with generous standalone $45: \u2248 $77.6 | with p=95%: \u2248 $81.8.\n  50% CI of IV: $70-80 | 80% CI: $60-85.\n  Margin of Safety = (75.1 \u2212 82.36)/75.1 = -9.7% \u2192 NONE.\n  Bayesian note: posterior p=85% is modestly BELOW the market's implied ~92-95% \u2014\n  the market has effectively already applied a 3:1 Bayesian update in the deal's\n  favor that I do not fully share (FCC consent is a real gating item; milestone\n  clauses can shave consideration).\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5. TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket-implied horizon: the price is set on a ~9-15 month deal-completion basis.\nMy fair-value horizon: 10 years (standalone) but the deal truncates it.\nSpread = My horizon \u2212 Market horizon \u2248 negative (market horizon SHORTER than the\n  standalone asset horizon, but the deal IS a terminal event for the public equity).\nNo positive horizon arbitrage: the $82.36 price does not embed multi-year earnings\n  growth; it embeds a near-term fixed payment. The reverse-arb check: if the deal\n  were removed, $82.36 would require ~$540M FY-2035 EBITDA (~60% margin on ~$900M\n  revenue) \u2014 UNREALISTIC standalone \u2192 confirms price \u2248 pure deal pricing.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nConviction scorecard (0-3 each, total 15):\n  1. Business quality:       2 (wide-but-narrowing moat; contracted revenue; weak cash economics)\n  2. Valuation attractiveness: 0 (negative MoS at T0)\n  3. Macro alignment:        1 (rates headwind, hawkish Fed)\n  4. Thesis clarity:         3 (deal price, conditions and KPIs are unambiguous)\n  5. Execution traceability: 3 (consent done, Apple agreements signed, filings visible)\n  TOTAL: 9/15 \u2192 MEDIUM (borderline High).\n  Conviction decay: -1 per 6 months without confirmatory events (FCC consent).\n  Note the split: confidence in the DEAL's mechanics is high; confidence in the\n  INVESTMENT's attractiveness at $82.36 is low. Net: do not size to High band.\n  Macro alignment (Section 1.4): Headwind \u2192 -0.5 steps, split entry (moot here \u2014\n  no entry).\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Short interest: 7.49% of float, 3.81 DTC, +28.3% MoM [Aggregator] \u2014 shorts\n  accumulating = a visible minority betting on deal-break/downside. Squeeze potential\n  low-moderate (insider block 59.5% removes most float).\n\u2022 Institutional ownership 27.2%; insider 59.5% (Thermo + Apple + mgmt) [Aggregator].\n  Apple is a SELLER at close (Licensee interest to Amazon sub) \u2014 aligned.\n\u2022 Options: not held \u2192 [Unconfirmed]. Sentiment: consensus targets cluster at $90\n  (mechanical deal target, not analytical) [Aggregator]. No contrarian signal.\n\u2022 Crowding risk score: 9/15 \u2014 deal-arb community and retail momentum are crowded\n  into the ~$82-90 band; position sizing -1%p where applicable.\n\u2022 Behavioral read: the +200% run from the 52w low into the deal embeds momentum +\n  FOMO; the current 8.5% \"deal gap\" is being treated as a riskless coupon. It is not.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Correlation profile: long-duration satellite/telecom = rate-sensitive, tech-\n  growth-like. Fits a small speculative allocation in a portfolio underweight\n  satellite/space; conflicts with any value/income sleeve.\n\u2022 Portfolio-level check: if the book already holds rate-sensitive long-duration\n  growth (e.g., other D2D/space names), GSAT adds correlated tail risk \u2014 the common\n  bear trigger is a broad risk-off/Fed-hike that both breaks risk appetite for\n  M&A timing AND discounts the standalone. Avoid if so; weight 0% recommended.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nBinary formulation at T0 (price 82.36; win = deal closes at ~$88 net, T\u224812mo):\n  Win p=0.85, payoff = (88\u221282.36)/82.36 = +6.8%\n  Lose q=0.15, payoff = (24\u221282.36)/82.36 = \u221270.9%\n  Kelly f* = (p\u00d7G \u2212 q\u00d7L)/L = (0.85\u00d70.068 \u2212 0.15\u00d70.709)/0.709 = (0.0578 \u2212 0.1064)/0.709 = \u22126.9% \u2192 NEGATIVE.\n  At p=0.90: f* = (0.0612\u22120.0709)/0.709 = \u22121.4% \u2192 still negative.\n  At p=0.93: f* \u2248 +0.7% \u2192 half-Kelly \u2248 0.4% (immaterial).\n  At p=0.95: f* \u2248 +4.1% \u2192 half-Kelly \u2248 2.0% (max defensible, and only in a pure\n  deal-arb sleeve with strict monitoring).\n  Kelly vs Conviction gap check (Layer 5 vs 6.5): Conviction band (Medium, up to\n  4-6% per framework) vs Kelly (0%) \u2192 gap >20pp \u2192 RE-ANALYSIS FLAG resolved by the\n  binary structure: the framework's Medium band assumes an operating company with\n  multiple return paths; GSAT is a one-outcome contract with negative expectancy\n  at T0. Kelly governs: SIZE = 0% for new money.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCatalysts (to monitor):\n  + FCC consent order for spectrum/licence transfer to Amazon (KEY \u2014 unlocks close)\n  + HSR early termination / clearance\n  + Milestone confirmations (MDA launch of 9 refreshment sats \"imminent\" [Estimate \u2014 Space Intel Report])\n  + Apple prepayment drawdowns toward $1.58B cap [Estimate]\n  + Q3-26/Q4-26 filings (still required until close)\n  + Any competing bid (probability low, ~5% [Assumption])\nRisks:\n  \u2212 FCC denial/conditioning of licence transfer (material; would de-risk the deal\n    premium); \u2212 milestone-adjustment clauses shaving consideration below $90;\n  \u2212 AMZN stock election value < $90 if AMZN falls below ~$280.37 (cap structure)\n    [Arithmetic on deal terms]; \u2212 deal-break \u2192 standalone $8-35; \u2212 single-customer\n    (Apple) renegotiation risk; \u2212 negative Q2-26 momentum (-$27M loss) worsening\n    standalone; \u2212 regulatory politics around Big-Tech M&A.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Common bear trigger: a risk-off episode / Fed hike (markets already price ~1/3\n  hike odds) would (a) push AMZN down (stock-elect value, though capped), (b) raise\n  the probability of regulatory delay/break for M&A broadly, (c) compress any\n  standalone valuation if the deal broke. Tail correlation with tech-growth longs\n  is HIGH in a hike scenario.\n\u2022 Conditional VaR: P(deal breaks) \u2248 15%; loss \u2248 \u221265% to \u221275%; CVaR(5%) \u2248 \u2212$55/share\n  vs price \u2192 expected tail loss \u2248 \u2212$8.3/share, only partially offset by the +$5.6\n  gain in the close case. Asymmetric risk profile confirmed.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nThesis: \"GSAT = $90 cash/stock consideration at ~85% probability, closing 2027.\"\nIntegrity thresholds:\n  1. DEAL KPI: FCC consent order issued \u2192 raise p to 95%, tighten close 