 Kelly-based max: 0% [Assumption].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nRisks:\n  1. Regulatory block/review delay (FCC, DOJ antitrust, CFIUS) \u2014\n     probability 4-16% (block + delayed)  [Assumption]\n  2. Satellite replacement deadline miss \u2014 2 launches scheduled late 2026\n     [Actual \u2014 SATNews]; launch slip is the most credible Amazon walk\n     trigger; probability 10-20% of a delay  [Assumption]\n  3. Amazon stock price collapse \u2192 stock election value falls; blended\n     consideration decreases. At AMZN $200, stock election = $64.20; at\n     $230, $73.83; at $280.37+, capped at $90  [Arithmetic; AMZN price\n     scenario = Assumption]\n  4. Cash/stock proration risk \u2014 high cash elections likely force some\n     shareholders into stock worth < $90. This is already embedded in my\n     $87 blended assumption; the real check is the merger agreement's\n     exact proration mechanics  [Unconfirmed]\n  5. Standalone failure-case downside: $45-55 (no fee) / $59.57 (with\n     fee); 33-45% loss from T0  [Assumption]\n  6. Time value: 4.71% 10Y \u2014 8.5% gross spread annualizes to ~10%, but\n     after failure probability the net expectation is negative  [Estimate]\n\nCatalysts (positive):\n  1. HSR (antitrust) early termination or close of review \u2014 could arrive\n     within 30-90 days  [Estimate]\n  2. FCC application filing and public comment close; FCC approval\n     (Chair Carr open-minded)  [Actual \u2014 CNBC/Ars]\n  3. Successful late-2026 launches (MDA/SpaceX)  [Actual \u2014 SATNews]\n  4. Public disclosure of cash/stock election results \u2192 near-certain\n     close confidence\n  5. Any competing bid (SpaceX previously held talks with GSAT in 2025)\n     [Estimate \u2014 Ars Technica]\n\nStep 7-4. PRE-MORTEM (5 years from now, why did this fail?)\n  Scenario A \u2014 \"Regulators killed it\": FTC sued to block on vertical\n    foreclosure theory (Amazon + Apple satellite exclusivity); FCC\n    designated a hearing. Deal died 2027; stock fell to $50; GSAT\n    standalone ran out of funding for C-3 and diluted shareholders.\n    Early warning indicators: DOJ second request (vs early\n    termination), FTC complaint filing, FCC hearing designation order.\n  Scenario B \u2014 \"Amazon walked\": GSAT missed C-3 launch milestones\n    (SpaceX/MDA delay); Amazon invoked the satellite-replacement\n    deadline condition; paid (or contested) $592M fee; stock fell to\n    $45-60. Early warnings: missed launch window announcements, 10-Q\n    going-concern language, fee dispute.\n  Scenario C \u2014 \"Apple squeezed the orange\": With Amazon gone, Apple\n    renegotiated capacity economics lower; GSAT revenue declined;\n    merger premium vanished; stock ~$40. Early warnings: Apple's\n    D2D investment in ASTS/other, contract amendments, falling\n    wholesale revenue.\n  Of the three, Scenario B is most probable (industry history of\n  launch delays is long).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n  \u2022 Common bear triggers across a portfolio: a regulatory \"Big Tech\n    backlash\" event would simultaneously (a) threaten the Amazon-GSAT\n    merger and (b) hit AMZN, MSFT, GOOGL, META holdings. Tail\n    correlation with tech-heavy portfolios: HIGH in that scenario.\n  \u2022 Rate shock: 10Y at 4.71% rising to 5.5%+ would reduce PV of deal\n    payoff by ~$1.30/share (87 \u2192 85.7) and pressure failure-case\n    multiples. Correlation with rate-sensitive portfolios: MODERATE.\n  \u2022 CVaR (5% conditional): worst 5% scenarios include regulatory block\n    or renegotiation \u2192 expected loss \u2248 -$32/share (-39%) on position\n    \u2192 for a 2% position: -0.78% portfolio CVaR contribution\n    [Assumption]. For 0% position: nil.\n  \u2022 VERDICT: systematic risk is moderate but real; the position adds\n    idiosyncratic binary risk without a compensating edge.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES & THESIS INTEGRITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n  Thesis integrity thresholds (deal-close thesis):\n  1. HSR/DOJ: if a Second Request issues \u2192 probability -10pct; if a\n     complaint is filed \u2192 thesis invalid; exit immediately.\n  2. FCC: if hearing designation order issues (rather than approval) \u2192\n     probability -10pct; if FCC approval with conditions (e.g., spectrum\n     divestiture) \u2192 probability +5pct; re-evaluate price.\n  3. CFIUS filing/clearance (if any): [Unconfirmed] \u2014 monitor.\n  4. Launch schedule: any delay of the two late-2026 launches past\n     2026Q4 \u2192 probability -5pct; past 2027Q2 \u2192 -10pct.\n  5. Amazon stock price: below $170 \u2192 stock-election value = $54.57,\n     blended value falls to ~$76 \u2192 probability of cash-heavy proration\n     shifts; re-evaluate.\n  6. Spread monitor: if price < $78 (spread > 15%) with no news,\n     reassess for a BUY (potential mispricing); if price < $75,\n     investigate news before buying.\n  7. Any 8-K referencing merger agreement amendment/termination \u2192 stop\n     and reevaluate immediately.\n\n  Decision Journal (Step 7-5 input \u2014 will be updated quarterly):\n  T0 2026-08-24, price $82.36, IV $81.49, P(close) 90%, failure value\n  $55, blended consideration $87, PV discount 5%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 9-1. Short Thesis (bear case on same data)\n  1. The $90 deal price is 4 months old; the stock at $82.36 already\n     prices ~90% close probability. The remaining 10% is systematically\n     underpriced for regulatory and launch-slip risks.\n  2. FCC leverage: Amazon faces an outstanding FCC dispute (its petition\n     against SpaceX's 1M-satellite application; Amazon's own Kuiper\n     deployment milestones were missed \u2014 Carr publicly criticized Amazon\n     for falling ~1,000 satellites short of its July 2026 milestone\n     [Actual \u2014 Ars Technica]). The FCC can extract major concessions\n     (milestone conditions, spectrum caps) that reduce Amazon's\n     willingness to close at $90.\n  3. GSAT's standalone business is worth $25-40 on fundamentals: TTM net\n     loss -$52M, revenue $281M, negative owner earnings (~-$82M),\n     62% gross margin but only 2.7% operating margin, net debt ~$100M,\n     and OCF inflated by Apple prepayments that are contractually owed.\n  4. Q2 2026 revenue declined -3.5% YoY and Q1 2026 EPS badly missed\n     (-$0.16 vs -$0.0952 consensus  [Estimate \u2014 web brief]) \u2014 business\n     momentum is NOT improving into the deal.\n  5. Amazon strategic optionality: Amazon can likely kill the satellite\n     project, pay a $592M breakup fee (~5% of deal value), and re-emerge\n     2-3 years later with a different D2D strategy (or an ASTS-like\n     partner), especially if consumer iPhone D2D monetization disappoints.\n  6. The cash/stock election structure at AMZN ~$252: holders electing\n     stock get ~$80.89, below the $90 cash; heavy cash elections force\n     proration and reduce realized consideration to $85.5-87.5. The\n     \"headline $90\" is a ceiling, not the median payout.\n  7. Short interest rising (+28.3% MoM) \u2014 informed capital is pressing\n     the deal-risk case.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic Combat (Long vs Short)\n  Long logic strength (deal closes): 8/10\n    \u2014 locked shareholder vote, Apple alignment, FCC openness, strategy\n      rationale.\n  Short logic strength (deal fails / underperforms): 5/10\n    \u2014 regulatory and milestone risk is real but low-probability.\n  Gap = 3 \u2192 conviction NOT downgraded further.\n  BUT: the long logic is fully PRICED at $82.36. A 8/10 thesis with a\n  0% expected risk-adjusted return does not justify a position.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial Data Sources\n  [Unconfirmed] \u2014 no Hindenburg/Bonitas-style report for GSAT was\n  retrieved. The GuruFocus SWOT and CSIMarket competitive data (GSAT\n  ~1.7% industry share vs Echostar 95.26%) were the most skeptical\n  third-party sources available  [Estimate \u2014 web brief]. No additional\n  adversarial report was located within research budget.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed Arguments\n  1. \"Thermo's 57.6% consent means the deal is done.\" \u2014 Killed because\n     shareholder approval was never the binding constraint; regulatory\n     approval and Amazon's willingness are. Thermo's consent is priced.\n  2. \"Apple cannot walk away; the contract runs to 2041.\" \u2014 Killed\n     because contracts can be amended/restructured; Apple publicly\n     supports AMAZON as the new provider \u2014 Apple's consent is a de-risker\n     for the deal, but if the deal fails, Apple is a monopsony\n     counterparty, not a protector of GSAT shareholders.\n  3. \"FCC Chair's comments make approval highly likely.\" \u2014 Partially\n     killed; Carr's public support is preliminary, non-binding, and\n     counterbalanced by the FCC's outstanding disputes with Amazon\n     (Kuiper milestones, anti-SpaceX petition, ~1,000-sat shortfall).\n  4. \"The stock is a free 9% return until close.\" \u2014 Killed by\n     PV-adjustment (5% discount \u2192 4% net spread), blended-consideration\n     haircut ($87 vs $90), and failure probability (~1% expected net\n     edge, negative on a risk-adjusted basis).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (MANDATORY)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n  A. Methodology Audit\n     A1. Engine 5 appropriate for binary merger-arb: PASS.\n     A2. No DCF-only conclusion: PASS.\n     A3. No peer-multiple-only conclusion: PASS.\n     A4. No narrative-only conclusion: PASS (all scenarios