.080 | +0.055 |\n2026-27 revenue growth anchors: Q1 2026 +17% [Actual], Q2 2026 \u22123.5% [Actual], FY2025 +9% [Actual]; post-2028 deceleration as Amazon Leo D2D [Actual 2028 deployment] competes with legacy Globalstar. WACC: 4.70% rf [Actual] + 1.514 beta [Aggregator] \u00d7 5.0% ERP [Assumption] \u2248 12.3% \u2192 use 11% blended with lower-scale premium [Assumption]. Terminal growth 2.5% [Assumption].\nPV of FCF 2026\u201330 \u2248 \u2212$0.44B; TV = 0.055\u00d71.025/(0.11\u22120.025) = $0.663B \u2192 PV \u2248 $0.39B; EV \u2248 \u2212$0.04B; add net cash $0.037B \u2192 equity \u2248 $0.0\u20130.1B. Pure cash-flow value \u2248 $0\u20131/share [Estimate].\nInterpretation: The DCF is a category failure for this asset class \u2014 it prices only cash flows, not spectrum scarcity, the 85%-capacity Apple franchise, or a strategic buyer's synergies. I retain it in the report to show that the $35\u201365 break-range rests entirely on strategic-asset premiums, NOT on earnings power. This is the critical model weakness and is carried into scenario widths.\n\nStep 3-2. Probability-weighted merger EV (Engine 5 \u2014 the primary engine):\n| Scenario | Probability [Estimate] | Per-share value ($) | EV contribution ($) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1. Close at $90, mid-2027 | 70% | 90.00 | 63.00 |\n| 2. Close at $90, delayed to 2028 | 10% | 84.00 (PV @9%) | 8.40 |\n| 3. Close at reduced consideration (AMZN < $280 or renegotiation ~$85) | 10% | 85.00 | 8.50 |\n| 4. Deal breaks; standalone trading | 10% | 48.00 (60% CI: 35\u201365) | 4.80 |\n| TOTAL | 100% | Expected Price | $84.70 |\nProbability anchors: base rate post-HSR \u2248 90% [Estimate]; my 80% total close is conservative; break value 48 = 0.35\u00d765 (second-bidder path, e.g., Apple or PE [Assumption]) + 0.65\u00d735 (strategic-standalone drift [Assumption]).\n\nStep 3-3. Reverse DCF (market-implied): At $82.36, with break value $48, market-implied close probability = (82.36\u221248)/(90\u221248) = 81.8% [Arithmetic]. My model says 80% close. The market is pricing the SAME odds I am \u2014 within noise. No free lunch.\n\nStep 3-4. Tornado (\u00b11\u03c3 on the top 3 variables):\n1. Close probability 70% \u00b110 \u2192 EV $80.5\u201388.9 (\u0394\u00b1$4.2) \u2190 THE driver\n2. Break value $48 \u00b115 \u2192 EV $83.2\u201386.2 (\u0394\u00b1$1.5)\n3. Time to close 10 mo \u00b16 \u2192 IRR 11.2% vs 7.9% gross (\u0394\u00b13.3% annualized)\nThesis KPI = FCC approval milestone (drives close probability).\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2022 Competitive response: if the deal closes, Amazon becomes the D2D anchor (Apple + Amazon), intensifying pressure on AST SpaceMobile/Starlink D2C \u2014 validates the spectrum thesis but does not change GSAT shareholder value (capped at $90) [Estimate].\n\u2022 Reflexivity: GSAT share price cannot improve the deal (fixed consideration). Declining AMZN < $241 makes the mixed consideration worth less than the GSAT price \u2014 a reflexive negative loop only in the stock-election tail [Arithmetic].\n\u2022 Customer evolution: Apple iPhone users unaffected; agreement survives via the Amazon\u2013Apple contract [Actual]. The 260K legacy subscriber base is immaterial to the deal.\n\u2022 Integration risk: MD Space liquidated-damages provision noted [Actual \u2014 10-Q]; satellite delivery delays are a deal-timing risk, not a value risk.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\nPrior (Layer 1.5): P(close) \u2248 87%. Likelihood updates: HSR cleared (+); majority consent (+); FCC pending (0); Amazon iRobot precedent (\u2212); Amazon+Apple political salience (\u2212). Posterior: P(close) \u2248 80% [Estimate].\nScenario discipline: probabilities sum to 100%; base case (close at $90) is the single highest probability \u2713.\n\u2022 Expected price: $84.70 [Estimate]\n\u2022 50% CI: $84\u201390 [Estimate]\n\u2022 80% CI: $48\u201390 [Estimate]\n\u2022 Margin of safety = (84.70 \u2212 82.36)/84.70 = 2.8% \u2192 LIMITED (<15%)\n\u2022 Expected IRR to mid-2027 close \u2248 (84.70/82.36)^(12/10) \u2212 1 \u2248 3.4% annualized; gross spread on base case = +9.3% absolute, ~11.2% annualized, minus 4.7% risk-free = ~6.5% risk premium for a 10-month binary [Arithmetic].\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2022 Market-implied horizon: ~10\u201316 months (deal close).\n\u2022 My default horizon: 3\u20135 years.\n\u2022 Spread: NEGATIVE \u2014 after close there is no equity. No horizon arbitrage exists; this is a maturity-transformation trade, not a compounding opportunity.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25