closes\" \u2014 no contrarian signal, but no edge either.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2022 Correlation profile: deal-break risk is idiosyncratic; modest correlation to AMZN and to Big Tech antitrust sentiment; low correlation to rates/commodities. Beta 1.514 [Aggregator] overstates market sensitivity in this regime.\n\u2022 In a 10\u201320-name portfolio: a 3% GSAT position contributes ~0.3% portfolio loss if the break scenario (\u221242%) hits \u2014 survivable, but the P&L is bounded +9%/\u221242%. Expected excess return (+2.8%) does not clear the portfolio's hurdle for event risk. Fit: MARGINAL.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2022 Edge b = $2.34 (EV 84.70 \u2212 price 82.36); odds = win $7.64 / lose $34.36 = 0.222\n\u2022 Full Kelly = edge/odds = 12.8% of capital; half-Kelly = 6.4%; with Model Confidence MEDIUM-LOW and left-tail uncertainty \u2192 25% Kelly = 3.2% [Assumption].\n\u2022 Layer 5 cap (3%) vs Kelly 3.2% \u2192 gap = 0.2pp (< 20pp rule \u2713). Final size: 3.0% max for existing holders; 0% new money (Layer 12).\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\nCatalysts (positive): FCC grant of spectrum/license transfer (primary); formal 2027 close guidance; AMZN strength > $280 (maintains cap); early-close signal from 8-K.\nRisks (negative): FCC denial/conditions; DOJ/FTC second-step action; AMZN sustained < $241 (mixed consideration < T0 price); Amazon strategic withdrawal (Leo cost overruns); MDA satellite delivery delays pushing close past 2028 \u2192 PV erosion.\nPre-mortem (WHY did this fail by 2028?):\n1. Regulatory kill: FCC designates the license transfer for hearing on public-interest grounds; competitor (SpaceX) lobbying successful. Early warning: FCC comment-period extensions, hearing designation orders.\n2. Amazon walk: Amazon Leo capital discipline review kills the deal; AMZN collapses < $200 on macro shock; Bezos/Jassy statements de-emphasize D2D. Early warning: AMZN 20%+ drawdown with Amazon Leo hiring freezes.\n3. Anti-Big-Tech politics: bipartisan legislation targets Amazon+Apple platform consolidation; state AGs intervene. Early warning: state AG announcements, congressional letters to FCC.\nDecision journal entry (Layer 7.5): T0 82.36; IV estimate 84.70; close prob 80%; break value 48; top assumption = FCC approval within 12 months; red-team concern = thin spread + binary tail.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK (PORTFOLIO VIEW)\n\u2022 Shared bear trigger: a broad risk-off selloff hitting AMZN (stock leg) while widening credit spreads on GSAT's $0.484B debt \u2014 in a \u22122\u03c3 equity event, AMZN < $230 \u2192 mixed consideration \u2248 $80\u201383, below the T0 entry; combined with deal-break repricing, CVaR at 95% \u2248 \u221235% to \u221245% [Estimate].\n\u2022 In the same regime, the standalone break value compresses (reduced M&A appetite) \u2192 correlation of the two legs rises exactly when the market crashes (tail correlation \u2248 0.6\u20130.8 [Assumption]). No hedge exists in GSAT itself; a short AMZN (0.3210\u00d7 notional) is the natural spread hedge but leaves the deal-break risk open.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY)\n1. FCC license transfer application granted \u2014 KPI TRIGGER: upgrade close probability to 90%; hold.\n2. AMZN daily close < $241 for 5 consecutive sessions \u2014 KPI: blended deal value < T0 price; model re-run; reduce or exit.\n3. Any filing indicating an extended FCC review (hearing designation, environmental/competition conditions) \u2014 exit immediately; the 10% break probability is back-weighted and expends capital.\n4. Company 8-Ks on merger timing each quarter: if expected close slips past Q2 2027 \u2014 revisit time-value \u2192 IRR < 6%; reduce.\n5. Earnings calls suspended [Actual] \u2014 quarterly revenue is NOT a deal signal; ignore financials for the trade.\nIf deal closes: sell or auto-convert (stock-election exposure = 0.3210\u00d7 AMZN capped at $90 \u2014 treat as capped; if you elect stock and AMZN > $280, you are long AMZN upside with no incremental value \u2014 do not hold past merger close).\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25