nue deceleration in Q2 2026 [Actual] and the strategic-value circularity described above.\nKilled arguments: \"Apple will buy GSAT if Amazon walks\" \u2014 killed: Apple just signed a 10-year-style capability agreement with Amazon [Actual \u2014 aboutamazon.com]; Apple buys services, not capex-heavy satellite fleets (hardware margins). Revives only IF the Amazon\u2013Apple agreement is itself renegotiated/terminated \u2014 not in base case.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (37-point framework, summarized)\nA. Methodology (pass): event-driven Engine 5 core with Engine 4 calibration; no DCF-only conclusion; no TAM narrative.\nB. Valuation (pass with caveat): cross-checked vs pre-deal price $72.85 [Arithmetic], reverse-DCF implied close probability 81.8%, sell-side $90 consensus \u2014 consistent.\nC. Bias (conditional pass): my close probability (80%) is BELOW market-implied (82%) \u2014 no overconfidence detected; break value admits wide CI (35\u201365) and is flagged assumption-heavy.\nD. Consistency (pass): all scenarios anchored to $90 or explicit fallbacks; no mixing of GAAP OCF with owner earnings (OCF corrected for prepayments/SBC).\nE. Narrative (pass): \"record revenue\" narrative correctly identified as irrelevant to a fixed-consideration deal; \"record OCF\" identified as a working-capital artifact [Arithmetic \u2014 accruals ratio \u22120.3123].\nF. Red team (pass): short thesis scored, conviction downgraded, pre-mortem written.\nG. Data integrity (FAIL on two items): AMZN spot price [Unconfirmed]; capex/FCC status [Unconfirmed]; vendor \"total debt $0.546B\" vs filed components $0.484B unresolved \u2014 I used filed components net of current portion; net debt conclusion (\u2248 \u2212$0.037B) robust to either definition. Also DISCARDED the csimarket claim that EchoStar holds 95% industry share [Unconfirmed \u2014 implausible; likely segment artifact]. \nModel confidence: MEDIUM-LOW (2 material data gaps + one unresolved vendor discrepancy).\nPass count: 33/37 evaluated items; 2 flagged fails, 2 not evaluable.\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\nDate: 2026-08-24 | T0: $82.36 | Expected value: $84.70 | MoS: 2.8% | Close prob: 80% | Break value: $48 (35\u201365) | Horizon: 10 months to decision | Key assumption: FCC grant within 12 months | Red-team flag: cash-flow value \u2248 $0\u20131/share; all break-scenario value is strategic-premium assumption | KPI: FCC filing grant; AMZN \u2265 $241 | Self-note: \"If the spread is not > 12% absolute, the trade is financing a binary risk at sub-high-yield yields. Re-entry only at \u2264 $78.\"\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\nACTION: HOLD (if owned) / AVOID (new money) at $82.36. NOT RATED as a compounder; correctly classified as an event-driven spread trade.\nCONVICTION: 7/15 (Medium-Low) \u2014 after red-team downgrade.\nWEIGHT: Existing positions \u2264 3.0% of portfolio; new positions 0% until price < $78.\nSTRATEGY:\n\u2022 At $82.36: risk-adjusted return is insufficient (expected IRR ~3.4% annualized; base-case gross spread 11.2% \u2212 4.7% rf = ~6.5% premium for a 10% \u221242% tail). The market has priced the same odds I can estimate. No edge.\n\u2022 Buy zone: \u2264 $78.00 \u2014 MoS \u2248 8.5%, spread \u2248 15.4% absolute, annualized IRR \u2248 19% (10-month close) \u2014 compensates for the binary tail at a 3% size.\n\u2022 Sell/trim zone: \u2265 $87.50 \u2014 spread < 2.9% absolute; cap the residual tail risk.\n\u2022 If held: do not elect all-cash reflexively; if AMZN > $280, cash and stock legs are equal. Elect cash, and avoid AMZN equity exposure post-close.\n\u2022 Hard exit triggers: FCC hearing designation; AMZN < $241 for 5 sessions; expected close pushed beyond Q2 2028.\n\u2022 Monitoring cadence: weekly 8-K/FCC check; recompute EV on any regulatory event.\n\nFINAL VERDICT: NEUTRAL \u2014 the market is paying a fair, thin price for a high-probability $90 outcome. The correct response is inaction: collect the spread if you already own it, do not reach for it with new capital, and do not mistake a 10-month capped arbitrage for an investment.\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nEND OF RS2 v2.0 ANALYSIS \u2014 GSAT (T0 2026-08-24)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25